      <room>AW1.126</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Back to the future, (re) learn smalltalk</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Smalltalk Devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A lot of the things in software engineering we take for granted these days are rooted in Smalltalk.&#xA;But most people do not program in Smalltalk. Do you wonder if there are more pieces of brilliance in Smalltalk waiting to be picked up by&#xA;the general computing community? Come and experience yourself.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We&amp;#39;ll work with you through an exercise showing Seaside, Glamour and other little known treasures, fully exploiting the &amp;#39;objects-all-the-way&amp;#39;&#xA;attitude visible in the Pharo open source Smalltalk environment.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Bring your laptop to pair through the exercises. Take home a web application, deployed on your laptop.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description></description>
      <persons>
          <person id="1821">Stephan Eggermont</person>
          <person id="1822">Willem van den Ende</person>
          <person id="1823">Diego Lont</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>